Here's the modified PHP code that retrieves the weather forecast for the next five days and displays the maximum and minimum temperature for each day in Celsius along with the average temperature for each day in a table format:
```php
<?php
$city = "YOUR_CITY_NAME";
$apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY";
$apiUrl = "http://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/forecast?q=" . $city . "&appid=" . $apiKey . "&units=metric";
// Make API request
$response = file_get_contents($apiUrl);
// Decode JSON response
$data = json_decode($response, true);
// Extract forecast data for the next five days
$forecastData = array();
$currentDate = null;
foreach ($data['list'] as $item) {
    $date = date('Y-m-d', $item['dt']);
    if ($date != $currentDate) {
        $currentDate = $date;
        $forecastData[$currentDate] = array(
            'description' => $item['weather'][0]['description'],
            'max_temp' => $item['main']['temp_max'],
            'min_temp' => $item['main']['temp_min'],
            'temp_sum' => $item['main']['temp'],
            'temp_count' => 1
        );
    } else {
        $forecastData[$currentDate]['max_temp'] = max($forecastData[$currentDate]['max_temp'], $item['main']['temp_max']);
        $forecastData[$currentDate]['min_temp'] = min($forecastData[$currentDate]['min_temp'], $item['main']['temp_min']);
        $forecastData[$currentDate]['temp_sum'] += $item['main']['temp'];
        $forecastData[$currentDate]['temp_count']++;
    }
}
// Output table header
echo "<table>";
echo "<tr><th>Date</th><th>Description</th><th>Max Temp (Celsius)</th><th>Min Temp (Celsius)</th><th>Avg Temp (Celsius)</th></tr>";
// Output table rows
foreach ($forecastData as $date => $item) {
    $avg_temp = round($item['temp_sum'] / $item['temp_count']);
    echo "<tr>";
    echo "<td>" . $date . "</td>";
    echo "<td>" . $item['description'] . "</td>";
    echo "<td>" . $item['max_temp'] . "</td>";
    echo "<td>" . $item['min_temp'] . "</td>";
    echo "<td>" . $avg_temp . "</td>";
    echo "</tr>";
}
// Close table
echo "</table>";
?>
```
Make sure to replace YOUR_CITY_NAME and YOUR_API_KEY with your own values. The code should output a table with the date, description, maximum temperature, minimum temperature, and average temperature for each day in Celsius.

