To create an interactive LaTeX document that prompts the user to input two numbers and select an operation, you can use the `hyperref` package to create input fields and radio buttons. Here is an example code that you can use:
```
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{hyperref}
\begin{document}
\begin{Form}
Enter the first number: \TextField[name=num1, width=3cm, format={var f = this.getField('num1'); f.value = f.value.replace(/[^\d.-]/,'');}]{}\\
Enter the second number: \TextField[name=num2, width=3cm, format={var f = this.getField('num2'); f.value = f.value.replace(/[^\d.-]/,'');}]{}\\
Select an operation: 
\ChoiceMenu[combo, name=operation]{}{Addition=subtraction,Subtraction=multiplication,Multiplication=division,Division=}
\medskip
\PushButton[name=calculate,onclick={%
var num1 = this.getField('num1').value;
var num2 = this.getField('num2').value;
var operation = this.getField('operation').value;
var result = '';
if (num1 && num2 && operation) {
  if (operation == 'Addition') {
    result = parseFloat(num1) + parseFloat(num2);
  } else if (operation == 'Subtraction') {
    result = parseFloat(num1) - parseFloat(num2);
  } else if (operation == 'Multiplication') {
    result = parseFloat(num1) * parseFloat(num2);
  } else if (operation == 'Division') {
    result = parseFloat(num1) / parseFloat(num2);
  }
}
this.getField('result').value = result;
}]{
Calculate
}
\medskip
Result: \TextField[name=result, width=3cm, readonly]{}
\end{Form}
\end{document}
```
In this code, the `TextField` commands create input fields for the user to enter the two numbers, with the `format` option ensuring that only numerical values are accepted. The `ChoiceMenu` command creates radio buttons for the user to select the operation, with the `combo` option allowing the user to type in the options or select from the drop-down list.
The `PushButton` command creates a button that, when clicked, runs a JavaScript function that calculates the result based on the user inputs and selected operation. The `parseFloat` function is used to convert the input values to numerical values, and the `if` statements check that all the required inputs are provided before calculating the result.
The `TextField` command at the bottom displays the result, with the `readonly` option preventing the user from editing the field.
