To create a table that lists all the sentences in the paragraph along with their character count, and sort the table in descending order based on the character count, you can use the following PHP code:
```
$paragraph = "The 2021 Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine was awarded to Gregory S. Mendel, a scientist who made several significant contributions in the field of genetics. He is best known for his discovery of the laws of heredity, which is the basis for modern genetics. Mendel's work laid the foundation for the study of genetics and revolutionized the field of biology.";
$sentences = preg_split('/(?<=[.?!])\s+/', $paragraph, -1, PREG_SPLIT_NO_EMPTY);
$table = array();
foreach ($sentences as $sentence) {
    $sentence = trim($sentence);
    $count = strlen($sentence);
    $table[] = array('sentence' => $sentence, 'count' => $count);
}
usort($table, function($a, $b) {
    return $b['count'] - $a['count'];
});
echo '<table>';
echo '<thead><tr><th>Sentence</th><th>Character Count</th></tr></thead>';
echo '<tbody>';
foreach ($table as $row) {
    echo '<tr><td>' . $row['sentence'] . '</td><td>' . $row['count'] . '</td></tr>';
}
echo '</tbody></table>';
