Can you create a PHP function that can classify sentences as either declarative or interrogative? 
Here's an example code you can use as a basis:
<?php
function sentenceType($sentence) {
    $lastChar = substr($sentence, -1);
    if ($lastChar == "?") {
        echo "The sentence is an interrogative sentence.";
    } else {
        echo "The sentence is a declarative sentence.";
    }
}
// Example usage:
sentenceType("How many stars are in the Milky Way?");
?>

output:
Sure! Here's a modified version of the code that uses regular expressions to classify sentences as declarative or interrogative:
```php
function sentenceType($sentence) {
    if (preg_match('/\b(who|what|when|where|why|how)\b/i', $sentence)) {
        echo "The sentence is an interrogative sentence.";
    } else {
        echo "The sentence is a declarative sentence.";
    }
}
// Example usage:
sentenceType("How many stars are in the Milky Way?");
```
This function checks if the sentence contains any of the interrogative pronouns (who, what, when, where, why, how) using a regular expression. If it does, then the sentence is classified as interrogative. Otherwise, it is classified as declarative.

