Here is a Java code solution to convert a negative sentence to a positive sentence:
```java
public class NegativeToPositive {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String negativeSentence = "I am not interested in that offer.";
        String[] words = negativeSentence.split(" ");
        StringBuilder positiveSentence = new StringBuilder();
        for (String word : words) {
            if (word.equals("not")) {
                continue;
            } else {
                positiveSentence.append(word).append(" ");
            }
        }
        positiveSentence.deleteCharAt(positiveSentence.length() - 1);
        positiveSentence.append(".");
        System.out.println("Negative sentence: " + negativeSentence);
        System.out.println("Positive sentence: " + positiveSentence);
    }
}
```
In this solution, we first split the negative sentence into individual words using the `split()` method. Then, we loop through each word and if we encounter the word "not", we simply skip it. For all other words, we append them to a `StringBuilder` object to build the positive sentence. Once we have looped through all the words, we remove the extra space at the end and add a period to complete the positive sentence. Finally, we print both the negative and positive sentences to the console.

