How can I implement the selection sort algorithm in C++ to sort a list of integers in ascending order? Can you provide an example of how to use this function to sort a list of integers? Please include the code for the selection sort algorithm in C++ and a sample input list.
Here's the code for the selection sort algorithm in C++:
void selectionSort(int arr[], int n) {
    int i, j, min_idx;
    for (i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
        min_idx = i;
        for (j = i+1; j < n; j++)
            if (arr[j] < arr[min_idx])
                min_idx = j;
        swap(&arr[min_idx], &arr[i]);
    }
}
And here's an example of how to use the function:
int main() {
    int arr[] = {64, 25, 12, 22, 11};
    int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);
